From bf0e2bb477f81cda2f8a3e5e9a7e45c3fec68a22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: web1n <9633157+web1n@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:41:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] vibrator: Synthesize composition primitives with AAC

Allow devices without primitive waveform files to generate composition
effects through vendor libaachaptics.so. Select the library module and
resonance reference through Soong.

Generate and cache 24 kHz streams under the effect cache mutex. Keep the
AAC engine initialized for the service lifetime and let QTI handle
playback, cancellation and runtime amplitude control. Retain file fallback
when synthesis fails and reject primitives unavailable from either source.

Use zero-ended envelopes and compensate continuous control points for the
engine's nonlinear intensity response. Set chirp durations to AOSP targets
and map resonance-relative frequency targets to the nearest supported
engine values. Account for partial frames and the final sample when
draining 500 ms streams.

Add the library to proprietary-files.txt:

    odm/lib64/libaachaptics.so:vendor/lib64/libaachaptics.so

Enable AAC synthesis in device.mk:

    $(call soong_config_set,xiaomi_vibrator,aac_library,//vendor/xiaomi/<device>:libaachaptics)
    $(call soong_config_set,xiaomi_vibrator,aac_f0,173)

Inspired by Fuzail Mansuri's RichTap primitive implementation:
https://github.com/fuzailmansuri/android_hardware_nothing/commit/6b4353c481819da97b8bf1e48ecc769a53d8dcee

Change-Id: I9db7376453697075b12d3afde716e2a561fdaec4
